# Build-context hygiene. `.env` holds CLERK_SECRET_KEY + PTERODACTYL_API_KEY and
# servers.json holds every game server's admin token; the build stage does `COPY . .`, so
# without this file both end up in an image layer - readable by anyone who can pull the
# image or run `docker save`, even though the app only ever reads them from the runtime
# environment. Next also copies a `.env` it finds here into .next/standalone, which the
# runtime stage then copies into /app, so excluding it here is the whole fix.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
servers.json
data/

# dependencies and build output are produced inside the image
node_modules
.next
out
*.tsbuildinfo

# local noise
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
